items.prompt:
Write one self-contained HTML file (plain JavaScript and a canvas, no libraries) that shows 20 balls bouncing inside a spinning heptagon:
- the heptagon rotates about its centre, one full turn every 5 seconds;
- all balls start at the centre and fall under gravity;
- the balls all have the same radius, are numbered 1 to 20, and each has a distinct colour;
- the balls bounce off the rotating walls realistically (the wall's motion affects the bounce) and collide with each other;
- friction makes the balls spin, and the spin is visible through the rotation of their numbers;
- the balls never leave the heptagon.
The animation starts by itself when the page loads and the heptagon is large enough to fill most of the window.

Write one self-contained HTML file (plain JavaScript and a canvas, no libraries) that shows 15 balls inside a slowly rotating hexagon that has a gap in one of its six sides:
- the hexagon rotates one full turn every 8 seconds, and the gap rotates with it;
- the balls fall under gravity, bounce off the rotating walls (the wall's motion affects the bounce) and collide elastically with each other;
- a ball that escapes through the gap falls off the screen and reappears at the centre 2 seconds later;
- each ball's colour shows its speed (blue for slow through red for fast);
- a counter in a corner shows how many escapes have happened.
The animation starts by itself when the page loads and the hexagon fills most of the window.
